  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Arch Bridge Light",
    "description": "A black-and-white lighthouse on a rock out in the water, reached only across a little stone bridge of three arches that the sea runs under. Its lantern and windows light up after dark in World View. 37 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Rock** — three dark Block 2x2s in an L make a rock standing out of the water, two blocks high, with Rocks round its foot; two of them flank the end of the bridge.\n2. **Shore** — two Wide Stairs (the upper one on a Brick 1x2, turned 90°, press **R**) climb onto a stone Block 2x2, the bridge's abutment.\n3. **Arch Bridge** — three Arches, two deep, carry a deck of Plate 2x2s a little wider than they are, with a Low Wall 2x1 along each side for a parapet. The sea runs through the arches.\n4. **Tower** — three Block 2x2s stacked white, black, white on the far side of the rock, so the bridge lands on open stone. The Door, turned 90°, faces the bridge; two Small Windows glow with lamplight at night.\n5. **Lantern** — a Round Plate 2x2 for the gallery, a Lantern that lights up after dark, and a black Hip Roof.\n\nStand it with the first step on the shore and the rest out over the water: the bridge is the only way across.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Rock: 3 Block 2x2, 6 Rock\n- Shore: 2 Wide Stair, 1 Brick 1x2, 1 Block 2x2\n- Arch Bridge: 6 Arch, 3 Plate 2x2, 6 Low Wall 2x1\n- Tower: 3 Block 2x2, 1 Door, 2 Small Window\n- Lantern: 1 Round Plate 2x2, 1 Lantern, 1 Hip Roof\n\n37 bricks in all.\n",
